  "body": "I need interval equivalent of `<meta http-equiv=\"refresh\" content=\"600;URL='#anyReminder'\" />`\r\nfor example `<meta http-equiv=\"refresh\" content=\"600;URL='#anyReminder';interval=yes\" />`\r\n\r\nIt doesn't work in intervals because there is no real reloading. hash-links don't reload site (according to spec) and the meta tag is not executed twice and nore. \r\n\r\nBusiness need: reminder without JS with use of CSS selector `:target` to show reminder without losing of not sent form data. \r\n\r\nIs there possibility to add it or any other proposed equivalent in HTML?",
